3. Once upon a time, the three little pigs—who had built houses of straw, sticks, and bricks—met Little Red Riding Hood on the forest path. She warned them that a wolf was prowling nearby. The pigs thanked her and hurried home. When the wolf came huffing and puffing, the straw and stick houses fell, but the brick house stood firm. Little Red Riding Hood, clever from her own encounter with the wolf, helped the pigs scare him away. Afterward, they shared apples and stories, and the forest was a little safer for everyone. [end of text]


